/**
 * @defgroup application_api Application API
 *
 * The API applications use to talk to Stripe.
 *
 * Everything here is framework agnostic. Pick an adapter to supply the
 * networking and web-server plumbing, then use these types for the actual
 * Stripe work.
 *
 * @sa @ref quickstart
 */

/**
 * @defgroup client Stripe Client
 * @ingroup application_api
 *
 * Creating customers, Checkout sessions, subscriptions, and billing portal
 * sessions.
 *
 * Start at StripeClient. It mirrors Stripe's own resource grouping, so
 * `customers()`, `checkout().sessions()`, `subscriptions()`, and
 * `billing_portal().sessions()` line up with the sections of Stripe's API
 * reference.
 *
 * @sa https://docs.stripe.com/api
 */

/**
 * @defgroup models Stripe Models
 * @ingroup application_api
 *
 * Plain structs describing the Stripe objects StripeKit returns.
 *
 * Each struct carries the fields StripeKit needs for billing and entitlement
 * decisions rather than every field Stripe returns. When you need something
 * that is not present, read it from the raw JSON in
 * stripekit::EventEnvelope::payload_json, or file a request.
 *
 * @sa https://docs.stripe.com/api
 */

/**
 * @defgroup webhooks Webhooks
 * @ingroup application_api
 *
 * Webhooks, are HTTP requests made by Stripe to our server to notify us of 
 * events (e.g., payment success). 
 *
 * Stripe can deliver the same event more than once whenever it cannot confirm
 * that you received it, so a webhook handler must be safe to run twice. The
 * types here do that for you: they check the signature, reserve the event id
 * in a store, and only then call your handler.
 *
 * @sa https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks
 */

/**
 * @defgroup errors Errors
 * @ingroup application_api
 *
 * The exceptions StripeKit throws, and the Stripe error details attached to
 * them.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup async Async Support
 * @ingroup application_api
 *
 * Coroutine and callback plumbing shared by the asynchronous client methods.
 *
 * Most applications only need to know that `*_async` methods return a
 * stripekit::Task that can be `co_await`ed.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup logging Logging
 * @ingroup application_api
 *
 * Routing StripeKit's diagnostics into the host application's log, with
 * helpers for keeping secrets out of log output.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup adapter_api Adapter API
 *
 * Adapters integrate StripeKit into a web framework (e.g., Drogon). They
 * provide the ability to send and receive HTTP requests to/from Stripe's
 * servers.
 *
 * An adapter supplies the two pieces of plumbing StripeKit deliberately does
 * not implement itself: outbound HTTPS requests to Stripe, and an inbound
 * route that receives webhook deliveries. Applications normally use a
 * ready-made adapter and never touch these interfaces.
 *
 * @sa @ref writing_an_adapter
 */

/**
 * @defgroup adapter_interfaces Adapter Interfaces
 * @ingroup adapter_api
 *
 * The abstract base classes an adapter implements.
 *
 * @sa @ref writing_an_adapter
 */

/**
 * @defgroup drogon_adapter Drogon Adapter
 * @ingroup adapter_api
 *
 * The adapter for the [Drogon](https://drogon.org/) web framework.
 *
 * @sa @ref writing_an_adapter
 */

/**
 * @defgroup version Version Information
 * @ingroup application_api
 *
 * Reading the StripeKit version and build metadata at runtime.
 */
